1067, 0.00023478108050767332], [5.270318433758803e-05, 0.00014326210657600313, 8.689286187291145e-05, 0.012896043248474598], [0.0005824005929753184, 0.0026101386174559593, 0.0020327779930084944, 0.011697829701006413], [0.0005119878915138543, 0.00018834980437532067, 0.008008837699890137, 0.004857605788856745]], "new_cot": "The question asks what is used for sensing visual things. Visual things are things that are seen with the eyes. The eyes are organs that are responsible for seeing things. The eyes have a part called the cornea that is responsible for sensing visual things. The cornea is a transparent layer that covers the front of the eye and helps focus light rays onto the retina. The cornea is the only part of the eye that is visible from the outside. The cornea is also the first part of the eye that light passes through when entering the eye. The cornea is made of collagen fibers that are arranged in a regular pattern. The cornea has no blood vessels and receives nutrients from tears and the aqueous humor. The cornea is also responsible for protecting the eye from dust, germs, and other foreign objects. The cornea is also responsible for refracting light rays and creating a clear image on the retina. The cornea is also responsible for sensing visual things because it contains nerve endings that send signals to the brain about the shape, size, color, and movement of objects. The cornea is also responsible for sensing visual things because it contains photoreceptors that convert light into electrical impulses that are sent to the brain. The cornea is also responsible for sensing visual things because it contains mechanoreceptors that detect pressure, touch, and vibration on the surface", "new_cot_probs": [2.5195246053044684e-05, 1.96220771613298e-05, 1.96220771613298e-05, 0.006165073253214359], "cot_prob": [-253.0], "cot_step_prob": [-89.5]}}}
